  'cli.help': '{app} ({latin}) — a lead plans and audits, an executor does the work (GPT, Claude, DeepSeek or WorkBuddy, each signed in on its own), in an automatic loop.\nThe command line keeps the old name: wbloop.\n\nUsage:\n  wbloop app                        open the desktop app (or the web interface if the app isn\'t built)\n  wbloop serve [--open] [--port N]  start only the local interface service\n  wbloop run [options] "goal"       run a new task in the foreground\n      -d, --dir <dir>               working directory (default: current directory)\n      --lead <gpt|claude|deepseek|workbuddy>   who plans and audits\n      --exec <gpt|claude|deepseek|workbuddy>   who does the work\n      --lead-model, --exec-model <model>   their models (--lead-effort, --exec-effort)\n      -m, --gpt-model <model>       GPT model (default: the best model the account can use)\n      --effort <low|medium|high|xhigh|max>   GPT reasoning effort (default high)\n      --wb-model <model>            WorkBuddy model (default auto)\n      --wb-effort <…|off>           WorkBuddy thinking effort (off = thinking off)\n      --wb-context <300k|1m|tokens> WorkBuddy context window\n      --team [auto|always]          Team Mode: GPT may split rounds across parallel WorkBuddy teammates\n      --teammates <N>               at most N teammates per round (default 3)\n      --mode <normal|plan|vuln>     plan = approve the plan before execution; vuln = vulnerability hunting\n      --lang <auto|en|zh|ja>        language the agents write in (default: the goal\'s language)\n      --max-rounds <N>              maximum rounds (default 30)\n      --budget <M>                  token budget in millions (GPT + WorkBuddy)\n      --check <command>             run after every round (e.g. "npm test"); the result goes to GPT\'s audit\n      --add-dir <dir,dir>           extra directories WorkBuddy may use\n      --web-search                  let GPT search the web\n      --no-review                   skip the independent review at the end\n      --ask                         let GPT pause to ask you (default: fully autonomous)\n      --start-at <23:00|time>       scheduled start\n      --goal-file <file>            read the goal from a file\n      --detach                      run in the background (survives closing the terminal)\n  wbloop resume <id|last> [--detach]   continue a stopped/interrupted/paused task\n  wbloop tail <id|last>             follow a task\n  wbloop msg <id|last> "message"     leave a message for GPT\n  wbloop approve-plan <id|last> [note]  approve the plan (Plan mode)\n  wbloop allow|deny <id|last> [request] [--always] [--reason …]   answer a sensitive-command request\n  wbloop compact <id|last>          WorkBuddy starts a fresh session with a summary next round\n  wbloop pause|stop <id|last>       pause / stop a task\n  wbloop list | show <id|last>      list tasks / show one\n  wbloop export <id|last>           export the conversation (Markdown, to Downloads)\n  wbloop usage [24h|7d|30d|12m]     token usage statistics\n  wbloop loop list | add [--run <id>] <spec> | cancel <id>   scheduled loops, e.g. loop add "daily 09:30 check the logs"\n  wbloop agents [--dir <dir>]       list WorkBuddy\'s sub-agents\n  wbloop prompt <lead|executor|teammate|reviewer|advisor>   print a built-in system prompt\n  wbloop quota                      GPT quota of the ChatGPT subscription\n  wbloop doctor                     check the engines, their sign-in and the setup\n  wbloop login <gpt|claude|deepseek|workbuddy> | logout <…>\n  wbloop config [key=value …]       view/change defaults, e.g. wbloop config ui.language=zh\n  wbloop templates [name]           list templates / print one (then use --goal-file)\n',

